        "question": "A 62-year-old man with known metastatic lung cancer presents with unilateral right leg swelling. On examination, the entire right leg is swollen, there is pitting oedema, and the calf is 5 cm larger than the left. He was bedridden for 4 days last week. He has tenderness along the deep venous system. What is his Wells score for DVT, and how should he be investigated?",
        "options": {
            "a": "Wells score 3 (moderate probability); perform D-dimer first",
            "b": "Wells score 5 (high probability); proceed directly to compression ultrasound",
            "c": "Wells score 7 (high probability); proceed directly to compression ultrasound",
            "d": "Wells score 2 (low probability); D-dimer to exclude DVT",
            "e": "Wells score 4 (moderate probability); treat empirically without imaging"
        },
        "correct_answer": "c",
        "explanation": "Wells DVT Score calculation: Active cancer (1 point), paralysis/immobilisation (1), bedridden >3 days (1), tenderness along deep veins (1), entire leg swollen (1), calf swelling >3 cm (1), pitting oedema (1), collateral veins (0 - not mentioned), alternative diagnosis likely (0 - no mention) = 7 points. Score ≥3 = DVT likely → proceed directly to compression ultrasound (no D-dimer needed).",
        "rationale": {
            "a": "Incorrect - score is higher; patient has 7 points (cancer + immobilisation + bedridden + tenderness + entire leg swollen + calf >3cm + pitting oedema)",
            "b": "Incorrect - score is 7, not 5 (missed some criteria), but management correct (ultrasound for high probability)",
            "c": "CORRECT - Wells score 7 (cancer=1, immobilisation=1, bedridden >3d=1, tenderness=1, entire leg=1, calf >3cm=1, oedema=1) = high probability → ultrasound",
            "d": "Incorrect - score is 7 (high probability), not 2; D-dimer only appropriate for low probability (score ≤1)",
            "e": "Incorrect - imaging required to confirm diagnosis before anticoagulation; empiric treatment without imaging not standard"
        },
        "key_learning_points": [
            "Wells DVT Score components (1 point each, except alternative diagnosis -2):",
            "• Active cancer (treatment ongoing or within 6 months) = 1",
            "• Paralysis/recent immobilisation lower limb = 1",
            "• Bedridden >3 days or major surgery <4 weeks = 1",
            "• Tenderness along deep veins = 1",
            "• Entire leg swollen = 1",
            "• Calf swelling >3 cm compared to other leg = 1",
            "• Pitting oedema (greater in symptomatic leg) = 1",
            "• Collateral superficial veins (non-varicose) = 1",
            "• Alternative diagnosis at least as likely = -2",
            "Score ≤1 (unlikely) → D-dimer; Score ≥2 (likely) → Ultrasound"
        ],
        "tags": ["respiratory", "DVT", "Wells score", "clinical prediction", "diagnosis", "week3"],
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "subspecialty": "Respiratory Medicine / Vascular Medicine",
        "citations": [
